1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:08,500
Let's start with a leek,
chopped nice and fine.

2
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:14,500
Then an onion, sliced
thin. Nothing fancy here.

3
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:20,000
The green pepper goes into the pan first.

4
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:25,500
Now the onion joins it.
Let them soften together.

5
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:31,500
Cook it slowly until
everything is soft and sweet.

6
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:37,500
Pour in the cream and let it warm up gently.

7
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:43,500
Stir in the blue cheese until it melts away.

8
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:49,500
The gnocchi only need a
minute in boiling water.

9
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:55,500
Bring the soft leek back
into the creamy sauce.

10
00:00:56,300 --> 00:01:01,500
Cut the cherry tomatoes in
half for some freshness.

11
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:07,500
Add the gnocchi to the sauce
and mix it all together.

12
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:13,500
Plate it up while it is nice and hot.

13
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:19,500
Finish with plenty of grated Gruyère.

14
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:25,500
And that's it. Creamy,
cosy and ready to eat.
